-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  dir_addincludepath.pcpp - Directive compliance: @addincludepath

  @addincludepath "<folder>"; adds a folder where the C/C++ compiler looks
  for #include files, for every translation unit of the build (BNF.md sec
  2). The folder must exist. @addincludepath may be given more than once
  (each folder is searched; one folder named again, in any spelling, is the
  same folder) and in an imported unit too: a unit adds to the one build
  (dir_addincludepath_byunit.pcpp shows that).

  This program adds res\tests\libs twice, in two spellings, and includes
  dir_addincludepath.h, which only res\tests\libs holds: the #include is
  found through the path alone. It prints what the header defines.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\dir_addincludepath.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\dir_addincludepath.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  EXPECT:
    dir_addincludepath_value() = 30
    DIR_ADDINCLUDEPATH_TWICE(21) = 42
    [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  EXITCODE: 0
  Both targets print the same; the [Heap] line is the debug build's heap report.

  Break it: run each file below the same way, without -r; each reports
  exactly what the // ERROR / WARN / HINT comment on its marked line says,
  and nothing else:
    dir_addincludepath_err_missing.pcpp   a folder that does not exist
    dir_addincludepath_err_file.pcpp      a file, not a folder
    dir_addincludepath_err_path.pcpp      a path no file routine can take
    dir_addincludepath_err_nopath.pcpp    dir_addincludepath.h included without
                                          @addincludepath: clang's error, at
                                          the #include line
*******************************************************************************/

module exe dir_addincludepath;
@addincludepath "$P:res/tests/libs";
@addincludepath "$P:res\\tests\\libs\\";

#include "dir_addincludepath.h"

begin
  println("dir_addincludepath_value() = {}", cpp("dir_addincludepath_value()"));
  println("DIR_ADDINCLUDEPATH_TWICE(21) = {}", cpp("DIR_ADDINCLUDEPATH_TWICE(21)"));
end.
